How format Flashdrive (Write protected error)

1. Check for a Physical Lock Switch
Some USB flash drives have a tiny switch on the side (like an SD card).
If it’s set to Lock, you won’t be able to format.

Slide it to Unlock, then try formatting again.

2. Remove Write Protection via Command Prompt (Diskpart)
⚠️ Careful: this will erase everything on the drive.
Press Win + R, type cmd, and press Enter.

Type:

 diskpart 
then press Enter.
List all disks:

 list disk
 (Find your flash drive by size.)

Select your flash drive:

 select disk X
 (Replace X with the correct number.)


Clear write protection:

attributes disk clear readonly
 
Now try formatting:

clean
create partition primary
format fs=ntfs quick
assign
exit

